2024-11-27 15:30:52,864  [processor_96_com.freshworks.ip.external.demo.hagrid.beans.JiraIssue] INFO  c.f.c.p.ProcessorTask#156 Get message {"clazz": "com.freshworks.ip.external.demo.hagrid.beans.JiraIssue", "key": "DEMO-8", "fields": {"summary": "Triaging requests into queues", "description": "Organise your customer's requests into queues to help your team stay focused while you keep track of what needs to be done. Build your own *queues* to split requests by agents, request types, office locations, status or your team's custom fields.\nh3. Try it out\nBuild a queue to show your recently resolved requests. Click *New queue* and update the status filter in *Issues to show* to only show requests set to *Resolved*.", "priority": {"name": "Medium"}, "issuetype": {"name": "IT Help"}, "creator": {"emailAddress": "himanshu@fwmstest.onmicrosoft.com"}}} from the kafka
2024-11-27 15:30:52,864  [processor_96_com.freshworks.ip.external.demo.hagrid.beans.JiraIssue] INFO  c.f.c.p.ProcessorTask#165 Checking which assets can be processed by this message from kafka
2024-11-27 15:30:52,864  [processor_96_com.freshworks.ip.external.demo.hagrid.beans.JiraIssue] INFO  c.f.c.p.ProcessorTask#156 Get message {"clazz": "com.freshworks.ip.external.demo.hagrid.beans.JiraIssue", "key": "DEMO-7", "fields": {"summary": "Automatically update linked requests", "description": "Automation rules let you automate repetitive tasks in your service project. For example, when a Jira issue gets transitioned, an automation rule updates its linked requests with a comment to show the assigned agent that it's changed.\n\nBuild your own automation rules to:\n\n* Resolve linked requests when a Jira issue closes.\n* Automatically update customers when a linked Jira issue transitions.\n* or add what whatever you like! Automation is flexible enough to keep you in control. \n\nVisit [our automation documentation to learn more|https://support.atlassian.com/jira-service-desk-cloud/docs/set-up-rules-to-automate-repetitive-tasks/].", "priority": {"name": "Medium"}, "issuetype": {"name": "IT Help"}, "creator": {"emailAddress": "himanshu@fwmstest.onmicrosoft.com"}}} from the kafka
2024-11-27 15:30:52,865  [processor_96_com.freshworks.ip.external.demo.hagrid.beans.JiraIssue] INFO  c.f.c.p.ProcessorTask#165 Checking which assets can be processed by this message from kafka
2024-11-27 15:30:52,865  [processor_96_com.freshworks.ip.external.demo.hagrid.beans.JiraIssue] INFO  c.f.c.p.ProcessorTask#156 Get message {"clazz": "com.freshworks.ip.external.demo.hagrid.beans.JiraIssue", "key": "DEMO-6", "fields": {"summary": "Linking requests to a Jira issue", "description": "If customers report a problem that you're tracking in Jira, you can link the requests to the Jira issue to consolidate information and automate progress updates.\n\n+Try it out+\n\nLinking requests works the same as it does in Jira issues.\n\n# Create a new link using the \ud83d\udd17Link issue button.\n# Select *\"is caused by\"* to link it to the root problem you're tracking in Jira. This lets us know to update linked requests with an internal comment when the issue transitions.\n# Search for the issue's key to link it with the request.\n\nVisit [our documentation to learn more|https://support.atlassian.com/jira-service-desk-cloud/docs/link-issues-together/].", "priority": {"name": "Medium"}, "issuetype": {"name": "IT Help"}, "creator": {"emailAddress": "himanshu@fwmstest.onmicrosoft.com"}}} from the kafka
