2024-11-27 16:28:47,896  [processor_99_com.freshworks.ip.external.demo.hagrid.beans.JiraIssue] INFO  c.f.c.p.ProcessorTask#156 Get message {"clazz": "com.freshworks.ip.external.demo.hagrid.beans.JiraIssue", "key": "DEMO-5", "fields": {"summary": "I need help connecting my laptop to the level 3 printer", "description": "I have been trying to print a document since 8am this morning but my laptop won't connect with the printer. I've restarted my laptop but it's still not working. If anyone has time to look soon, I'll be at my desk for most of the day.", "priority": {"name": "Highest"}, "issuetype": {"name": "Service Request"}, "creator": {"emailAddress": "himanshu@fwmstest.onmicrosoft.com"}}} from the kafka
2024-11-27 16:28:47,896  [processor_99_com.freshworks.ip.external.demo.hagrid.beans.JiraIssue] INFO  c.f.c.p.ProcessorTask#165 Checking which assets can be processed by this message from kafka
2024-11-27 16:28:47,896  [processor_99_com.freshworks.ip.external.demo.hagrid.beans.JiraIssue] INFO  c.f.c.p.ProcessorTask#156 Get message {"clazz": "com.freshworks.ip.external.demo.hagrid.beans.JiraIssue", "key": "DEMO-4", "fields": {"summary": "Collecting custom request details", "description": "Define and organize incoming requests using *request types*. Capture and track relevant details upfront by customizing the *request types* you want to show up on the Help Center. You can also add *internal fields* to track details that you don't want your customers to see.\n\nh3. Try it out\n\nWe've given you some request types to try. Visit *Channels* (you may need to click *Back to project* to get out of your queues menu) to raise a request via your service project's Help Center and see them in action.", "priority": {"name": "High"}, "issuetype": {"name": "Service Request with Approvals"}, "creator": {"emailAddress": "himanshu@fwmstest.onmicrosoft.com"}}} from the kafka
