2024-11-27 16:28:47,897  [processor_99_com.freshworks.ip.external.demo.hagrid.beans.JiraIssue] INFO  c.f.c.p.ProcessorTask#156 Get message {"clazz": "com.freshworks.ip.external.demo.hagrid.beans.JiraIssue", "key": "DEMO-3", "fields": {"summary": "Agents & customers", "description": "*Agents* are the members of your team that answer and resolve requests from your *Customers*. In Jira Service Management, you only pay for agents and not the customers who raise requests. In other words, you can support as many customers as you need without paying any extra.\n\nReady to invite your team? Look for *Invite team* on your project's sidebar to the left (you may need to click *Back to project* to get out of your queues menu) to invite your team as agents.", "priority": {"name": "Highest"}, "issuetype": {"name": "IT Help"}, "creator": {"emailAddress": "himanshu@fwmstest.onmicrosoft.com"}}} from the kafka
2024-11-27 16:28:47,897  [processor_99_com.freshworks.ip.external.demo.hagrid.beans.JiraIssue] INFO  c.f.c.p.ProcessorTask#165 Checking which assets can be processed by this message from kafka
2024-11-27 16:28:47,897  [processor_99_com.freshworks.ip.external.demo.hagrid.beans.JiraIssue] INFO  c.f.c.p.ProcessorTask#156 Get message {"clazz": "com.freshworks.ip.external.demo.hagrid.beans.JiraIssue", "key": "DEMO-2", "fields": {"summary": "Capturing customer email requests", "description": "The easiest way for your customer's to request help is by sending an email request to your service project. When emails get sent to your project, they land in your queue as a request (just like this one).\n\nh3. Try it out\n\nEmail a request to *Demo service project's* support email address ( [mailto:demo@freshworks-ip.atlassian.net] ) to see how it looks for your customers and agents.", "priority": {"name": "Medium"}, "issuetype": {"name": "Service Request"}, "creator": {"emailAddress": "himanshu@fwmstest.onmicrosoft.com"}}} from the kafka
