2024-11-27 16:28:47,912  [processor_99_com.freshworks.ip.external.demo.hagrid.beans.JiraIssue] INFO  c.f.c.p.ProcessorTask#156 Get message {"clazz": "com.freshworks.ip.external.demo.hagrid.beans.JiraIssue", "key": "DEMO-7", "fields": {"summary": "Automatically update linked requests", "description": "Automation rules let you automate repetitive tasks in your service project. For example, when a Jira issue gets transitioned, an automation rule updates its linked requests with a comment to show the assigned agent that it's changed.\n\nBuild your own automation rules to:\n\n* Resolve linked requests when a Jira issue closes.\n* Automatically update customers when a linked Jira issue transitions.\n* or add what whatever you like! Automation is flexible enough to keep you in control. \n\nVisit [our automation documentation to learn more|https://support.atlassian.com/jira-service-desk-cloud/docs/set-up-rules-to-automate-repetitive-tasks/].", "priority": {"name": "Medium"}, "issuetype": {"name": "IT Help"}, "creator": {"emailAddress": "himanshu@fwmstest.onmicrosoft.com"}}} from the kafka
